{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/replacingaregistry"]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSets"}],"title":"Replacing a hand-written registry","role":"article"},"sections":[],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","anchor":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking"],"generated":true}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A registry is a list someone has to keep in step with the code: every analytics event type in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array, every route in a table, every dependency registered in one function at startup. A new type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that isn’t added works everywhere except where the list is read, and nothing tells you. Moving the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list onto LinkerSets takes four steps, and the list is deleted at the end."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Take an analytics library whose events are types conforming to ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsEvent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", collected by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hand so the library can validate their schemas at launch:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public protocol AnalyticsEvent {","    static var name: String { get }","}","","\/\/ Every module's events, listed by hand.","let allEvents: [any AnalyticsEvent.Type] = [","    Login.self,","    Logout.self,","    PurchaseCompleted.self,","]"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"1. Give the library a macro","anchor":"1-Give-the-library-a-macro","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Pick a kind (“evnt” is ","type":"text"},{"code":"0x6576_6E74","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","type":"reference"},{"text":" explains) and add a compiler plugin","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose macro requires the protocol, so its records hold ","type":"text"},{"code":"any AnalyticsEvent.Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Analytics.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The library declares the macro and the kind, and re-exports LinkerSets for the expansion:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@_exported import LinkerSets","","extension LinkerSetKind {","    public static let events = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x6576_6E74)","}","","@attached(peer)","public macro Event() = #externalMacro(module: \"AnalyticsMacros\", type: \"EventMacro\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The LinkerSetsMacroSupport module’s documentation has the package targets this needs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"2. Read the set beside the list","anchor":"2-Read-the-set-beside-the-list","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Before touching any event, read both and compare them, in a test or a debug build:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let discovered = LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values","let missing = allEvents.filter { listed in !discovered.contains { $0 == listed } }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"missing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" starts as the whole list and shrinks as events are marked."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"3. Mark each event where it’s declared","anchor":"3-Mark-each-event-where-its-declared","type":"heading","level":3},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@Event","struct Login: AnalyticsEvent {","    static let name = \"login\"","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event that doesn’t conform fails to compile. A generic event type, or one nested in a generic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type, is refused with a message, as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" lists; such a type needs its concrete"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specializations listed by hand, or a concrete wrapper."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"4. Delete the list","anchor":"4-Delete-the-list","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"missing"},{"type":"text","text":" is empty, the library reads the set instead:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let allEvents = LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"and the hand-written array goes. A new event is registered by writing ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":" on it, in whichever","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"module declares it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Other registries","anchor":"Other-registries","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The same steps fit any list whose entries can be declared as constants, functions or types:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Routes","type":"text"}]},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Route static let profile = Route(path: \"\/profile\")"},{"text":", read as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet<Route>"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Migrations"}]},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Migration static func addUsers(_ db: inout Database)"},{"text":", read as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet<(inout Database) -> Void>"},{"text":", sorted by a version the migration declares.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Dependency registrations","type":"text"}]},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Registration static func register(_ container: Container)"},{"text":", each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"module registering its own factories, read and called once at startup.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A registry whose order matters gets it from the entries, never from the set: the linker’s order is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stable but not one you choose ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Move a central list of event types, routes or registrations onto declarations that find"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"themselves."}],"references":{"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/FindingRecords":{"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/findingrecords","title":"Finding records","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Read every declaration of a kind, as the type you expect."}]},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/WhatTheMacrosRefuse":{"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/whatthemacrosrefuse","title":"What the macros refuse","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","abstract":[{"text":"Every declaration a record can’t describe is a compile error, with a message that says why.","type":"text"}]},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/DeclaringAKind":{"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/declaringakind","title":"Declaring a kind","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","abstract":[{"text":"Pick the number that tags your declarations, and decide whether your users write it.","type":"text"}]},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/PlatformsAndLinking":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/platformsandlinking","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where records are found, how, and which test shows it."}],"kind":"article","title":"Platforms and linking","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets":{"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets","title":"LinkerSets","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declarations that register themselves at compile time and are found at run time across every module a program links."}]}}}